# R541A GA3 / GA4: static standing clock
KA: Fe-56 binding energy per nucleon from the table: 8.7903 MeV (textbook 8.790)
KA: hydrogen b = m_p/m_H = 0.999456 (textbook 0.999456)
b (mode nucleon): Ti 1.009113, Pt 1.008294, TA6V 1.009089, PtRh10 1.008363, Be 1.006685
b (mode A m_u): Ti 1.001077, Pt 1.000183, TA6V 1.001054, PtRh10 1.000256, Be 0.998648
Delta b: Ti - Pt = 8.1900e-04;  TA6V - PtRh10 = 7.2576e-04;  Be - Ti = -2.4281e-03
Q - 1 = -Phi/c^2 in the standing state: Earth at MICROSCOPE altitude 6.263e-10; Sun at 1 AU 9.871e-09

## footing canonical: alpha (naive GA1 value) = 0.84399
  (i-a)/(i-c) as needed: eta(TA6V,PtRh10) = -4.121e-03, eta(Ti,Pt) = -4.650e-03 -> x6.64e+11 the bound; MU swap Pt->Be: eta(Be,Ti) = 1.372e-02; gamma_eff - 1 = 1.093e+01 -> x1.63e+05 the Cassini bound
  (i-a)/(i-c) MU alpha/2: eta(TA6V,PtRh10) = -5.333e-04, eta(Ti,Pt) = -6.018e-04 -> x8.60e+10 the bound; MU swap Pt->Be: eta(Be,Ti) = 1.783e-03; gamma_eff - 1 = 1.464e+00 -> x2.19e+04 the Cassini bound
  (i-a)/(i-c) KA alpha=0: eta(TA6V,PtRh10) = 0.000e+00, eta(Ti,Pt) = 0.000e+00 -> x0.00e+00 the bound; MU swap Pt->Be: eta(Be,Ti) = 0.000e+00; gamma_eff - 1 = 0.000e+00 -> x0.00e+00 the Cassini bound
  (ii) beta = 0.84399: b_T = 1 for every stationary body -> eta = 0 (classical); gamma_eff - 1 = 2 beta/(1-beta) = 1.082e+01 -> x1.61e+05 the Cassini bound
  (i-b) at alpha = 1: eta(Ti,Pt) = 2 alpha Delta b |Phi|/c^2 = 1.719e-11 (Earth + Sun potential only) -> alpha <= 4.07e-04
  GA4 as needed: law form kept (same mu); deep-regime v^4 = (1-alpha)^3 G M a0 = 0.1560 x G_lab M a0 -> a0_eff/a0 = 0.1560; |a0_eff/a0 - 1| = 0.844 vs 0.10 line
  GA4 MU alpha/2: law form kept (same mu); deep-regime v^4 = (1-alpha)^3 G M a0 = 0.5780 x G_lab M a0 -> a0_eff/a0 = 0.5780; |a0_eff/a0 - 1| = 0.422 vs 0.10 line
  GA4 KA alpha=0: law form kept (same mu); deep-regime v^4 = (1-alpha)^3 G M a0 = 1.0000 x G_lab M a0 -> a0_eff/a0 = 1.0000; |a0_eff/a0 - 1| = 0.000 vs 0.10 line

